<title>CANADA: Bid target Merfin stock heavily traded.</title>
<headline>Bid target Merfin stock heavily traded.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in takeover target Merfin International Inc were heavily traded on Wednesday after the specialty paper maker urged shareholders to accept a sweetened bid from Buckeye Cellulose Corp.</p>
<p>Merfin shares were up 0.05 at 7.45 on volume of 909,100 shares in Toronto.</p>
<p>Memphis-based Buckeye raised its offer to C$7.50 a share from C$7 after rival Polymer Group Inc of South Carolina on Tuesday increased its bid to C$7.20 from C$7.15.</p>
<p>Polymer said on Wednesday it was withdrawing its offer.</p>
<p>Merfin makes air-laid paper for use in products such as diapers and pre-moistened towlettes.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
</text>
